# Supabase project settings (Settings -> API in the Supabase dashboard)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_ANON_KEY

# Optional local-only convenience. When the Supabase URL is loopback, the login screen can fill
# the six demo accounts using the same password shape as scripts/create-users.ps1. Never set this
# in a production Pages environment.
VITE_DEMO_PASSWORD_SEED=

# Server-only contract for the submit-price-list Edge Function: Supabase injects
# SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY as function secrets.
# Never create a VITE_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY or otherwise expose the service key to the browser.
# Configure APP_BASE_URL and/or the comma-separated ALLOWED_ORIGINS secret so browser CORS is
# restricted to the deployed application origins.
# The public supplier portal additionally requires a random server-only value of at least 32
# characters as SUPPLIER_PORTAL_RATE_LIMIT_PEPPER. It HMACs client IPs before the persistent
# database rate limit; never prefix it with VITE_ and rotate it only with an explicit rollout.

# Federated sign-in, per provider. These are BUILD-TIME flags: Vite substitutes them into the
# bundle, so a deploy that omits one ships a product with that provider silently absent — the
# button is not drawn at all, even when the provider is fully configured server-side in Supabase
# Auth. That is exactly what happened on 25.08.2026: Google was enabled and working in the
# project, and the live site offered no Google button for hours because the deploying environment
# did not carry this variable.
#
# Enabling one here is NOT enough on its own. The provider must also be enabled in Supabase Auth
# with its client id and secret; the flag only decides whether the product offers the door.
# `true` (the literal string) enables; anything else, including unset, disables.
VITE_GOOGLE_SIGNUP_ENABLED=
# Apple has never been exercised — no Apple Developer Program membership, so no Service ID and no
# signing key (#269). Leave empty until that exists.
VITE_APPLE_SIGNUP_ENABLED=

# Web Push (optional) — the PUBLIC half of the VAPID pair; safe in the browser bundle by
# design. Generate the pair with `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`; the PRIVATE half goes
# only to Edge Function secrets (deploy steps: supabase/migrations/0016_push_triggers.sql).
# Leave empty to disable the push UI ("לא מוגדר בסביבה זו" in Settings).
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=

# Optional licensed Almoni Neue production build. Never commit font binaries or license secrets.
SUPPLYFLOW_ALMONI_FONT_DIR=
SUPPLYFLOW_ALMONI_400_SHA256=
SUPPLYFLOW_ALMONI_500_SHA256=
SUPPLYFLOW_ALMONI_600_SHA256=
